**Trade-offs.** Route splitting reduces initial bytes and improves time-to-interactive, at the cost of: one more round trip on first navigation to each route (mitigated by prefetch), the `ChunkLoadError` class of bugs, and complexity around shared chunks (a bug-fix to a shared dependency invalidates every chunk that uses it, so you want long-lived vendor chunks and immutable hashed filenames). The failure mode of over-splitting is worse than under-splitting on a fast connection and better on a slow one â€” so measure on the slowest network your users actually have (4.6.8 RUM, not lab).

